    "bio": "a Representative from South Carolina; born in Halifax County, N.C., in 1770; moved to Mountain Shoals (now Enoree), S.C.; received a limited education; held several local offices; member of the South Carolina state house of representatives; elected as a Democratic Republican to the Fifteenth and to the two succeeding Congresses; reelected as a Jackson Republican to the Eighteenth Congress; and reelected as a Jacksonian candidate to the Nineteenth and to the two succeeding Congresses (March 4, 1817-March 3, 1831); died in Mountain Shoals (now Enoree), S.C., January 3, 1834; interment in the private burial ground on the family estate west of Enoree, S.C.",
